{
  "_comment": [
      "The frames the gateway puts on the GT86 / ADU bus and the signals in them. tools/generate.py turns this,",
      "plus ToyotaLens's data/{engine,ect,abs}.json, into src/uds/uds_definitions.cpp, src/translator_table.cpp",
      "and gt86-bus.dbc / isf-bus.dbc. Edit this file, run the generator, never edit the generated files.",
    "DBC signal names get the frame's first name token as a prefix (ENG_, TRANS_, ABS_, GT86_, ISF_), so the ADU channels are unique across frames and sort by source module; 'name' here is the bare signal name.",
    "'adu' on a signal names the built-in ADU channel it feeds (ecu.clt, ecu.rpm, ...): the CANX files carry it as the channel's override, so the ADU's stock pages and warnings use the gateway's value. At most one signal per file per built-in channel.",
      "",
      "Every signal is little-endian; startBit is the bit position of its least significant bit (byte*8 + bit).",
      "A signal without 'factor' is pass-through: the ECU's raw value goes into the frame unchanged, its width",
      "comes from the ToyotaLens mask, and the DBC carries ToyotaLens's scale factor and offset. A signal with",
      "'factor' (and 'bits') is re-encoded: raw = (physical - offset) / factor, the way the GT86 modules expect.",
      "'blockByte' copies one byte of a Mode 21 block into one frame byte, every flag keeping its bit position.",
      "",
      "GT86 packets: ids, default bytes and the layouts below were taken from captures of the real GT86 bus in",
      "gt86-isf-swap/logs/GT86 (cluster_working_no_errors.txt for the bytes; the two-minute drive for the",
      "layouts: 0xD1 and 0xD4 at 0.0565 km/h per bit, 0x141 bits 32-45 engine rpm, 0x360 bytes 2-3 oil and",
      "coolant temperature minus 40). Intervals are the rates seen in the drive capture.",
      "",
      "ADU frames: 0x5E0-0x5E7, the only band empty on the GT86 bus (its traffic spans 0x018-0x4DD, 0x63B,",
      "0x6E1-0x6E2 and the 0x7xx diagnostic ids).",
      "",
      "'broadcast': frames the IS F modules send on their own (no request). Their signals are parameters of",
      "module 'isf' that an output frame references by uniqueId like a Mode 21 parameter, and they are decoded",
      "the moment the frame arrives, so the GT86 motion frames do not wait for a poll. startBit follows the DBC",
      "convention ('order' big = Motorola @0, start bit is the MSB; little = Intel @1, start bit is the LSB),",
      "so a line can be copied from a Toyota DBC. Scaling checked against gt86-isf-swap/logs/ISF_SPEED_RPM_driving.csv."
  ],
  "broadcast": [
    {
      "id": "0x0B0", "name": "ISF_ABS_FrontWheelSpeeds", "module": "abs", "rate": "63 Hz", "length": 6,
      "comment": "Toyota ABS front wheel speeds, FR then FL, 0.01 km/h per bit (TOYOTA_LEXUS.dbc 0xAA order; no offset on this generation)",
      "signals": [
        {"uniqueId": "isf.0B0.WheelSpeedFR", "name": "FR Wheel Speed (ABS broadcast)", "startBit": 7, "bits": 16, "order": "big", "factor": 0.01, "offset": 0, "unit": "km/h"},
        {"uniqueId": "isf.0B0.WheelSpeedFL", "name": "FL Wheel Speed (ABS broadcast)", "startBit": 23, "bits": 16, "order": "big", "factor": 0.01, "offset": 0, "unit": "km/h"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "0x0B2", "name": "ISF_ABS_RearWheelSpeeds", "module": "abs", "rate": "63 Hz", "length": 6,
      "comment": "Toyota ABS rear wheel speeds, RR then RL, 0.01 km/h per bit",
      "signals": [
        {"uniqueId": "isf.0B2.WheelSpeedRR", "name": "RR Wheel Speed (ABS broadcast)", "startBit": 7, "bits": 16, "order": "big", "factor": 0.01, "offset": 0, "unit": "km/h"},
        {"uniqueId": "isf.0B2.WheelSpeedRL", "name": "RL Wheel Speed (ABS broadcast)", "startBit": 23, "bits": 16, "order": "big", "factor": 0.01, "offset": 0, "unit": "km/h"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "0x0B4", "name": "ISF_ABS_Speed", "module": "abs", "rate": "63 Hz", "length": 8,
      "comment": "Toyota vehicle speed, bytes 5-6 big-endian, 0.01 km/h per bit (TOYOTA_LEXUS.dbc SPEED 47|16@0+); byte 7 checksum",
      "signals": [
        {"uniqueId": "isf.0B4.VehicleSpeed", "name": "Vehicle Speed (ABS broadcast)", "startBit": 47, "bits": 16, "order": "big", "factor": 0.01, "offset": 0, "unit": "km/h", "adu": "ecu.speed"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "0x2C4", "name": "ISF_Engine_RPM", "module": "engine", "rate": "30 Hz", "length": 8,
      "comment": "Toyota engine rpm, bytes 0-1 big-endian signed, 0.78125 rpm per bit (TOYOTA_LEXUS.dbc ENGINE_RPM_2 RPM 7|16@0-)",
      "signals": [
        {"uniqueId": "isf.2C4.EngineRPM", "name": "Engine Speed (ECU broadcast)", "startBit": 7, "bits": 16, "order": "big", "signed": true, "factor": 0.78125, "offset": 0, "unit": "rpm", "adu": "ecu.rpm"}
      ]
    }
  ],
  "toyotaLensData": "../../ToyotaLens/data",
  "frames": [
    {
      "id": "0xD0", "name": "GT86_GSensor", "gt86": true, "interval": 100, "defaults": "00 00 01 00 00 00 00 00", "comment": "Steering angle and lateral/longitudinal G; default bytes only: wheel straight, no G (the real car at rest sends 0E 00 01 00 00 00 00 FF)"
    },
